.TH "PB-CONFIG-CONFLICT-SHOW" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-config-conflict-show - Show a current path conflict


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb config conflict show <environment> <path> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Show a current path conflict

.PP
Display the path, reason and current status for one environment conflict. Use compare to read the actual machine and repository content before choosing which version to keep with resolve.

.PP
Conflicts identify exact paths whose local and repository versions cannot be merged automatically. Review the affected path before choosing a side; resolution records a deliberate decision for the next synchronization step.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for show

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-config-conflict(1)\fP
